        "<p>This field equation defines the Einstein curvature tensor \\( G_{\\mu\\nu} \\) in terms of the Ricci tensor \\( R_{\\mu\\nu} \\), the Ricci scalar \\( R \\), and the metric tensor \\( g_{\\mu\\nu} \\), which are sourced by the stress-energy tensor \\( T_{\\mu\\nu} \\). Under this general relativistic framework, the local mass-energy density \\( \\rho \\), pressure \\( P \\), and momentum flux \\( J^i \\) act as the source of geometry, proving that curvature and matter are dynamically married. By representing these field equations through tensor calculus, the formalism guarantees that the physical predictions remain covariant under general coordinate transformations \\( x^\\mu \\to x'^\\mu \\), ensuring that general relativity holds across all reference frames.</p>"
